Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat:=20beta.8=20=E2=80=94=20native=20on-device?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20speech=20engine=20(sherpa-onnx=20+=20NVIDIA=20parakeet-tdt-0?=
 =?UTF-8?q?.6b-v2)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Recorder transcripts move from whisper-base.en WASM (~12% WER, 30-min cap) to
NVIDIA parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2 int8 (CC-BY-4.0, ~6% WER — above whisper-large-v3
on the Open ASR leaderboard) running in an Electron utilityProcess via
sherpa-onnx-node. Measured on this M-series Mac: 66.6s lecture in 3.4s
inference (~20x realtime), so refine now covers up to 3h recordings.

- electron/asr-worker.ts: utilityProcess child hosting the engine (warm reuse,
  jobs serialized); electron/nemesis-asr.ts: one-time ~480MB model download to
  userData/asr with streamed progress + disk-space guard, worker lifecycle
  (2-min idle kill), nemesis:asr:transcribe IPC.
- Renderer: native-asr.ts bridge; refineTranscript and the Recordings
  Transcribe button go native-first with the existing WASM path as fallback
  (which keeps its 30-min cap). Audio still never leaves the machine.
- Build: asr-worker bundled as third esbuild entry; sherpa-onnx-node +
  sherpa-onnx-darwin-arm64 staged into dist/node_modules like node-pty
  (also in before-pack for per-target builds).
